# Day 38/50 — Servers

Every time we open a website, send a request or access an online service, something somewhere needs to respond.

That's where **servers** come in

A server is a computer or software system that provides services or resources to other devices, known as clients.
It might store website files, process requests, manage databases or deliver information.

We usually notice the result — a webpage loading or a file appearing — but not the system working behind it.

And that's what makes servers interesting.

A lot of important work happens without demanding attention.

**Not everything that keeps things running needs to be seen.**
